xt\":\"The 429 refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\"},{\"text\":\"The Retry-After header's value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely.\",\"line\":11,\"span\":\"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely, so waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the refusal names the window the gateway counted in.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"The body of the refusal is JSON, and it names what the gateway calls the “window” it counted in.\"},{\"text\":\"The body of the refusal names the cap and the tier.\",\"line\":13,\"span\":\"It names the cap and the tier as well.\"},{\"text\":\"There are four rules for retrying, given in the order they should be applied.\",\"line\":17,\"span\":\"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway computes the wait on the 503 path as well as on the 429 path.\",\"line\":19,\"span\":\"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 200 wants nothing.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 429 wants the stated wait.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 500 may be retried once the stated wait has passed.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A 503 is the overload path.\",\"line\":21,\"span\":\"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\"},{\"text\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"A batch credential is measured over exactly the same window as the default tier.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\"},{\"text\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued and cannot be asked for per call.\"},{\"text\":\"The tier cannot be asked for per call.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued and cannot be asked for per call.\"},{\"text\":\"Nothing about the two tiers differs other than the allowance.\",\"line\":23,\"span\":\"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\"},{\"text\":\"The log line for a refusal should carry the credential, the window and the wait.\",\"line\":25,\"span\":\"The log line should carry the credential, the window and the wait.\"},{\"text\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons, only one of which is the cap.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons and only one of them is the one above.\"},{\"text\":\"A credential may be suspended.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\"},{\"text\":\"A route may be closed for maintenance.\",\"line\":29,\"span\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\"},{\"text\":\"A request body may exceed the 5 